{"repositoryId":1340413376,"availability":"available","full":"Shubin123/vslam_gym","name":"vslam_gym","description":"Vision-driven locomotion demo: a car steers itself around a three.js track from the rendered image, using ONNX Runtime Web on WebGPU for steering regression and YOLOv8 detection.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-20T07:29:25Z","updated":"2026-09-23T22:40:02Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://shubin123.github.io/vslam_gym/","topics":["computer-vision","onnxruntime","opencv","self-driving","threejs","webgpu","yolov8"],"demo":"https://shubin123.github.io/vslam_gym/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T13:45:20.894Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T13:45:20.894Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T13:45:20.894Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T23:48:13.256Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-19T13:45:20.894Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A locomotion demo using ONNX and three.js framebuffers for computer vision.","A virtual car drives itself around a 3D track by looking at the rendered image; the scene is rendered, read back out of the canvas, and fed to two neural networks running in the browser: one predicts a steering angle from the road ahead, the other detects objects in the same frame.","The track is generated rather than loaded: a closed loop of cubic Bézier segments, built in the page from src/core/bezier-track.js. Because the centreline is known, how much of the track has been driven is a measured number rather than something inferred from the shape of the journey, which is what turns a run into an attempt that can be scored, failed and retried."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Shubin123/vslam_gym/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4e03efc46cefce06c2fa4b75969a12e223621ae1adbcba4397195c3997cce8c5","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:13.369Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:13.369Z","pro